Upstream describes its hardware field code as ported from hekate-math.

This modified, independent C++/Metal implementation adds 32-bit carryless
arithmetic, nibble lookup linear transforms, a cached five-permutation prefix,
candidate-only GPU output and offline validation/build harnesses. It is not an
upstream release. The Python reference is intentionally bit-serial and uses
dense matrices to independently check the optimized arithmetic and transforms.

Public pool vectors and protocol documentation:
https://noid.suprnova.cc/stratum/noid-poseidon2b-vectors.json
https://noid.suprnova.cc/stratum/stratum-protocol.md
https://noid.innovlab.cc/
Pool fixtures are unchanged source data; generated fixtures only normalize the
header/nonce layout. One upstream flat_mul_samples entry labels square(b) as
square(a); tests document the discrepancy rather than changing the source.
No proprietary miner code or binaries are incorporated.
